course: dictionary
lesson: 8019
title: Refill and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Refill can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to refill something means to fill it again after it has become empty. «Refill your bottle» tells you to fill it up once more.
explain: As a noun, a refill is a second filling or a new supply. «Free refills» means the café will fill your cup again without charging you. «An ink refill» is a new supply of ink for a pen.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. Ask yourself: is someone doing the action, or is it a thing? Then swap in your meaning, "fill it again," and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Refill means to fill something again after it has become empty.
fact: A refill can also be a noun: a second filling, or a new supply for something.
fact: «When you flush, a valve opens and water from the cistern rushes into the bowl.» The cistern refills, and a float shuts off the water when it is full.
fact: «Visitors may take sweets, the pile shrinks, and the gallery refills it.» Here refills is a verb, because the gallery is doing the action.
fact: An extractor spins honey out of the uncapped cells, saving the wax comb so the bees can refill it.
exercise: «When the bottle is empty, you can refill it at the tap.» What does refill mean here? | Throw it away and buy a new one | Drink it all at once | Put the lid on tightly | *Fill it again after it has become empty
exercise: «The café offers free refills of tea.» What is a refill in this sentence? | *A second filling of tea, given free | A cup that has been broken | A jug that is too heavy to lift | A small tin for storing tea
exercise: «The bees can refill the comb once the honey is out.» Find and copy the word that means fill again. | bees | honey | comb | *refill
test: «Please refill the tank before the trip.» What does refill mean? | Sell it to a friend | Paint it a new colour | Empty it completely | *Fill it again
test: Jayden says, «I need an ink refill.» What is an ink refill? | Water for a flower vase | A notebook full of blank paper | A pen with no ink at all | *A new supply of ink for a pen
exam: The café sign says «Free refills!» What does this mean? | Free drinks that you must pay for later | A new café opening next week | *A second filling of your drink at no extra cost | A cup with a crack in it
